01:20:52,173 --> 01:20:58,173
Da 5 Bloods is a 2020 American war drama film directed,
produced, and co-written by Spike Lee.

13
01:27:36,521 --> 01:27:42,521
It stars Delroy Lindo, Jonathan Majors, Clarke Peters, Johnny Trí Nguyễn, Norm Lewis, Isiah Whitlock Jr., Mélanie Thierry, Paul Walter
Hauser, Jasper Pääkkönen, Jean Reno, and Chadwick Boseman (in his final film role to be released during his lifetime).

14
01:34:20,869 --> 01:34:26,869
The film's plot follows a group of four aging Vietnam War veterans who return to the country in search of the
remains of their fallen squad leader, as well as the treasure they buried while serving there.

15
01:41:05,217 --> 01:41:11,217
Originally written by Danny Bilson and Paul De Meo in 2013, the script was re-worked by Lee and
Kevin Willmott following the pair's successful collaboration in BlacKkKlansman (2018).

16
01:47:49,565 --> 01:47:55,565
The cast joined in February 2019 and filming began a month later,
lasting through June and taking place in Southeast Asia.

17
01:54:33,913 --> 01:54:39,913
With a production budget of $35–45 million, it is
among Lee's most expensive films.

18
02:01:18,260 --> 02:01:24,260
Da 5 Bloods was released by Netflix on June 12, 2020.

19
02:08:02,608 --> 02:08:08,608
It received acclaim from critics, who praised the direction, themes, and the performances of
Lindo, Peters and Boseman, with many considering it among Lee's best works.

20
02:14:46,956 --> 02:14:52,956
The film received numerous accolades, including nominations for the Academy Award for Best Original Score and Screen Actors Guild Award for
Outstanding Performance by a Cast in a Motion Picture, and was named by the National Board of Review as the Best Film of 2020.

